# REST API Design Conventions

## Versioning
All APIs are versioned: `/api/v1/{resource}`. Bump to `v2` for breaking changes; maintain `v1` until all tenants migrate.

## Idempotency-Key header
All POST endpoints that create or mutate state **must** accept and honour the `Idempotency-Key` header. Return `200 Already Processed` for duplicate keys.

```java
@PostMapping("/ingest/training-attendance")
public ResponseEntity<?> ingest(
    @RequestHeader("Idempotency-Key") String idempotencyKey,
    @RequestHeader("X-Tenant-ID") String tenantId,
    @RequestBody @Valid TrainingAttendanceBatch batch) { ... }
```

## Standard error response shape
```json
{
  "status": 422,
  "error": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
  "message": "attendance_percentage must be between 0 and 100",
  "traceId": "abc123",
  "tenantId": "tenant_acme_corp",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-28T08:00:00Z"
}
```

## OpenAPI annotations
Every controller method must have `@Operation(summary = "...")` and `@ApiResponse` annotations. The API spec is published automatically to the Kong Developer Portal.

## Tenant headers
Never read `tenantId` from the request body or path. Always read from `X-Tenant-ID` header set by Kong. Reject requests missing this header with `400 Bad Request`.

## HTTP status codes
- `200` — idempotent duplicate or successful read
- `201` — resource created
- `202` — async work accepted (ingest, report generation, erasure requests)
- `422` — validation failure (include `errors[]` array)
- `409` — conflict (e.g. duplicate rule name within tenant)
- `429` — rate limit exceeded (include `Retry-After` header)
- `503` — circuit breaker open (include `Retry-After`)

## Pagination
All list endpoints must support `?page=0&size=20&sort=createdAt,desc`. Never return unbounded lists.
